# --- Personal financial data -------------------------------------------
# Your actual positions: quantities, average costs, P&L, tax lots.
# Deliberately excluded even from a private repo. A private repo can be made
# public by a misclick, collaborators added later see the whole history, and
# git history is permanent -- removing a committed file needs a history
# rewrite. The framework works with any holdings file, so the data does not
# need to live in the repo at all.
config/holdings.csv
config/holdings.csv.bak
data/holdings.json
.env

# --- Large generated data ----------------------------------------------
# market.db is ~450MB; GitHub rejects files over 100MB and this is entirely
# reproducible with run_market_ingest.py.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/cache/

# --- Fetched / derived config ------------------------------------------
# All regenerable, and stale within days. NOTE: git does not support inline
# comments in .gitignore -- a trailing "# note" becomes part of the pattern
# and the file silently stays tracked. Comments go on their own lines.
#
# config/fundamentals.csv <- fetch_fundamentals.py
# config/equities.csv, config/etfs.csv <- instruments.snapshot()
# config/watchlist.csv <- seeded from the NIFTY index lists
config/fundamentals.csv
config/equities.csv
config/etfs.csv
config/watchlist.csv

# --- Environment and noise ---------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
logs_*.txt
nohup.out
